hi i'm danny ceo and welcome to a new  episode of do  just one thing  and you know what the motto is it's  bananas  and what we're talking about today is  one of my favorite fruits but we're not  talking about the fruit inside of the  peel  we're actually talking about banana peel  so  believe it or not banana peel is edible  and if you go online you can find a  whole assortment of crazy  delicious recipes that use the banana  peel so what we're going to make today  is something called banana peel tea and  it's a one  step recipe that is delicious and it's  going to be  something that i think will become your  favorite sleepy time  bedtime tea to drink every single night  so first and foremost you want to  wash the bananas so make sure there's no  dirt no chemicals nothing on the outside  that's going to really  impact the taste of your tea and what i  like to do is first  eat the fruits and then i take one  banana peel so this is a fresh banana  peel and so if i have the banana in the  morning  what i'll do is i'll actually just put  it in a teacup just like this  and i fill it up all the way on the  inside you can cut it in half if it's a  smaller cup  and then it's as simple as this taking  hot water  and pouring it all over the banana peel  you're steeping it you're making a  regular tea and the funny thing about  banana peel tea  is that it doesn't taste like bananas  it's kind of a beautiful  herbal slightly sweet tea  and the reason that i love banana peel  tea is that if you think about it  bananas are high in potassium and  magnesium so this is infusing a ton of  potassium but also the magnesium  which is known to really help with aches  and pains  so if you really want to have the best  sleep of your life i highly suggest  making a little banana peel tea steep it  for about five to ten minutes and then  take out your banana peel and what i  like to do  is also dress it up so you can add a  splash  of your favorite milk or in this case  i'm using  a macadamia nut milk a little splash of  honey  if you want to do agave syrup or brown  sugar and then all you have to do  is enjoy  mmm really really good don't forget if  you want to tag this banana peel tea  recipe in your social media  use the drew barrymore show in your tag  and also be sure to check out more  videos and ideas and recipes at the  jukeberrymart thejuveberrymartshow.com  plus  be sure to pick up my magazine  naturallydannyco  now on newsstands
 

